On Sun, 19 Oct 2003 00:00, M. Pender wrote:
> I'd like to suggest that we put the name of the user group to a vote at the
> first meeting.
>
> I think we can do better than SELUG -- it is too likely to be pronounced
> "slug" which suggests that the operating system is slow and unresponsive.

http://www.slug.org.au/
The name SLUG seems reasonably popular.  It also stands for the Sydney Linux 
Users Group.

Having the name of the area in the title is a good idea though as there will 
probably be quite a number of SE Linux users' groups around the world soon.

> As an alternative, I'd like to suggest "Capital Area Security Enhanced
> Linux" user group--pronounced "castle" user group--which suggests a
> fortress or stronghold designed to keep out intruders.

If you make a mention of Security Enhanced X in the group title then I'm sure 
you would get more interest.

